{"ratings":[{"id":"F1","consequence":"secret","trigger":"unusual","reason":"A rare catalogue-key failure combined with a concurrent private observation can expose that observation to an agent."},{"id":"F2","consequence":"outage","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A tab-leading private detail and a long whitespace run can block the daemon's event loop for a quadratically increasing period."},{"id":"F3","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"normal","reason":"Ordinary multiline private assertions can cause unrelated code to be redacted, leading an agent to review an inaccurate change."},{"id":"F4","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"unusual","reason":"An unusually large catalogue can remain in memory until replacement, but the cache retains only one catalogue per store and no exhaustion was demonstrated."}]}